# Cell from playpick: mode=daily, boss=saved (coverage label only -- a daily's
# boss is drawn from the UTC date, not choosable), spec=warlock:destruction,
# style=auto, view=1280x800, save=fresh.
#
# Probe (2026-09-27-6-probe.play) found today's daily is The Three Crowns,
# 25-player normal, SWARMING -- the same boss+affix combination this line has
# already fought four times on 2026-09-26 (two melee, one idle, one good, all
# on touch views) plus a direct mode=raid dodge pull. Not chasing the crown
# mechanic again for its own sake -- direction.md already has that story from
# every style except wander. What is actually new here: this is the first
# mode=daily session on a non-touch viewport (all eight prior daily sessions
# used a touch view) and the first warlock on any daily.
#
# style=auto on a view without ",touch" is a known driver-lesson fallback:
# src/main.ts's isTouchMode() gate means the AUTO toggle can never be tapped,
# so scripts/playbot.ts's own no-autocast-toggle rule plays it as `good`
# instead. Confirmed twice before (mage:frost, druid:feral) but never yet
# inside mode=daily specifically -- this fills that gap rather than
# re-deriving the mechanism.
#
# The daily's class grid is index-only (class:0..class:16, not named specs);
# probe's targets/screenshot confirms class:14 is "Warlock" (Warlock has one
# spec, destruction, per src/sim/classes.ts's SpecId list) and its button is
# "start", not "pull".
open
tap daily
tap class:14
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot open

play auto 90
bill
state
shot mid1

play auto 90
bill
state
shot mid2

play auto 90
bill
state
says
shot end

play auto 30
bill
state
says
shot finish
